A pipe item's title comes from the config, when it names one.

A pipe has no tags of its own, so the fixup titles it with its file
name, and that is what the speakers, the Home app and Control Center
show until the writer's metadata arrives: "spotify.fifo". The new
library option `pipe_title` gives every pipe item that title instead,
unset by default, so the file can keep a file name and the listener
still reads a word.

